From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:21:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: offer macOS's highlight recovery
 setup on T8132

In a dark room this camera's picture turns magenta, a green deficit that
grows with the sensor gain. Side by side with macOS's own session on the
same Mac, one of the settings macOS sends and the driver does not is
highlight recovery: HR_ENABLE (0x1005) with 0, 0 early on, and late in
the setup SIFR_SKIP_INTERVAL_SET (0x1008) at 1 followed by HR_ENABLE
with 0, 1. macOS's frame metadata then reports highlight recovery on,
with a gain-down ratio, so it changes how the gain is split.

Add macos_hr to send that sequence at stream start, with a helper for
the settings that take two words after the channel. It is off by default
until a dark-room test shows its effect.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cmd.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index bbd2853ab6..49dd07e3db 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -1284,6 +1284,45 @@ module_param(macos_face_detect, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(macos_face_detect,
 		 "Turn on face and body detection as macOS does on this camera (default: off)");
 
+/* A setting with two words after the channel. */
+static int isp_ch_u32x2_set(struct apple_isp *isp, u16 opcode, u32 ch, u32 a,
+			    u32 b)
+{
+	u32 buf[5] = { [3] = a, [4] = b };
+
+	return isp_cmd_ch_raw_get(isp, opcode, ch, buf, sizeof(buf));
+}
+
+/*
+ * macOS turns on highlight recovery on this camera every session, late in
+ * the setup: HR_ENABLE (0x1005) with 0, 0 first, then the raw skip interval
+ * at 1 (SIFR_SKIP_INTERVAL_SET, 0x1008) and HR_ENABLE with 0, 1. Its frame
+ * metadata then reports highlight recovery on, with a gain-down ratio. The
+ * driver leaves both at the firmware's defaults. How the gain is split
+ * bears on the low-light colour cast, so macos_hr offers macOS's sequence
+ * for tests (default: off).
+ */
+static bool macos_hr;
+module_param(macos_hr, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(macos_hr,
+		 "Turn on highlight recovery as macOS does on this camera (default: off)");
+
+static void isp_ch_macos_hr(struct apple_isp *isp, u32 ch)
+{
+	int err;
+
+	if (!READ_ONCE(macos_hr) || !isp->hw->macos_session_settings)
+		return;
+	err = isp_ch_u32x2_set(isp, CISP_CMD_CH_HR_ENABLE, ch, 0, 0);
+	if (!err)
+		err = isp_cmd_ch_u32_set(isp, CISP_CMD_CH_SIFR_SKIP_INTERVAL_SET,
+					 ch, 1);
+	if (!err)
+		err = isp_ch_u32x2_set(isp, CISP_CMD_CH_HR_ENABLE, ch, 0, 1);
+	if (err)
+		dev_warn_once(isp->dev, "highlight recovery refused: %d\n", err);
+}
+
 /*
  * A floor on the auto exposure gain (1/256 steps, as AE_GAIN_CAP_SET), for
  * tests: with it a lit scene is taken at the sensor gain of a dark room,
@@ -1867,6 +1906,7 @@ static int isp_ch_configure_capture(struct apple_isp *isp, u32 ch)
 	isp_ch_macos_face_detect(isp, ch);
 	isp_ch_ae_gain_min(isp, ch);
 	isp_ch_desk_view(isp, ch);
+	isp_ch_macos_hr(isp, ch);
 
 	if (READ_ONCE(macos_be_la) && isp->hw->macos_session_settings) {
 		err = isp_cmd_ch_be_lasetting_set(isp, ch, isp_macos_be_la);
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cmd.h b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cmd.h
index 52032c63fd..51249cd1c6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cmd.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cmd.h
@@ -108,6 +108,8 @@
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_FACE_DETECTION_ENABLE		     0x0d05
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_AE_CONTROL_BODY_DETECTION		     0x0249
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_BODY_DETECTION_CONTROL		     0x5006
+#define CISP_CMD_CH_HR_ENABLE				     0x1005
+#define CISP_CMD_CH_SIFR_SKIP_INTERVAL_SET		     0x1008
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_LTM_MODE_SET			     0x2004
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_LTM_GAMMA_SET			     0x200a
 #define CISP_CMD_CH_FID_START				     0x3000
-- 
2.43.0

